cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZRay in academic work, please cite the paper below."
title: "ZRay: Portable Compiler-Assisted Memory Traffic Characterization"
abstract: >-
  ZRay is an LLVM compiler pass and runtime that characterizes the memory traffic
  of developer-marked regions of interest. It separates the statically knowable
  instruction mix of each region from sampled dynamic execution counts, recovering
  per-region loads, stores, bytes moved and bandwidth without hardware performance
  counters and without per-access binary instrumentation.
